A brief history of !ArcLink5
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Versions below 1.00 are beta-test versions.


v0.13a    (13th Jun 1999)
          a) Fixed bug where ArcLink5 occasionally locked up when
             directly transferring a file from the Psion into a
             RISC OS application such as Pipedream.
          b) Added translation where SHIFT-SPACEs are converted to
             normal spaces when converting Word files into Text
             files.
      
v0.13     (13th Jun 1999)
          a) Re-coded main display window so that full details
             are given instead of large icons.
          b) Fixed a couple of bugs to stop you trying to delete
             'open' files on the Psion.
          c) MAJOR NEW ADDITION - Added rudimentary file conversion
             to save Acorn text files as 'Word' files on the Psion
             and vice versa.
          d) Error no longer given if you try to create a directory
             which already exists on the Psion.
          e) Fixed bug whereby replacing a file on the Psion
             now updates the Acorn filer display correctly, rather
             than adding a second entry.
          f) Added code to prevent two copies of ArcLink5 running
             at once.
          g) Made sort on Name case-insensitive.
          h) MAJOR NEW ADDITION - Added recursive, hiararchical
             copying from the Acorn to the Psion.
          i) Added some more error checking conditions.
          j) Added support for more Psion error messages.
          k) Added support for !SparkFS so that you can drag
             archives to ArcLink5 to automatically extract the
             files into a new directory.
          l) MAJOR NEW ADDITION - Added rudimentary file conversion
             to read OPL files from the Psion and convert them to 
             Acorn text files.

v0.12     (17th Nov 1998)
          a) Fixed silly bug where I forgot to reset the baud
             rate correctly when you saved choices and then
             re-loaded them. This created serial frame errors
             next time you loaded ArcLink5.
          b) Extended serial delay slightly to allow for the
             Psion opo file to quit correctly when you have
             changed the baud rate and then quit the Acorn end.
          c) Re-designed the Psion.opo file for additional
             screen clarity, including current baud rate display.

v0.11     (10th Nov 1998)
          a) Fixed bug where ArcLink5 failed to set the correct
             baud rate on loading, if a different baud rate was
             saved in the choices.
          b) Fixed bug where serial ports other than 0 (on fast
             (serial port cards) failed to work correctly.
             
v0.10     (30th Oct 1998)
          a) Made slight alteration to registration code.
          b) Adjusted so that Risc OS version is read correctly,
             even if you have installed the new window manager
             on pre Risc PC machines.
          c) Serial port is only reset when if exit, if you've
             actually contacted the Psion, else ArcLink5 should
             exit neatly.
          d) Amended block driver initialisation so that any
             remaining problems should be fixed.
          e) Added error logging (if 'debug' turned on) so that
             any errors are logged in the ArcLink5 scrap dir.
          f) Initialisation/error handling updated to allow
             ArcLink5 to turn off SerialDevs if choices were 
             saved to on, and then ArcLink5 reloaded with no
             Serial card present.
          g) Modified date reading routines so that additional
             modules such as "SensibleTime" should work ok.
          h) Amended to allow faster baud rates than 19200 on
             A5000 machines with Atomwide Serial cards fitted.
          i) Amended ArcLink5 to only work at 9600 baud until
             registered.

v0.09     (2nd Sep 1998)
          a) Tidied up !SerialDev routines so that ArcLink5 is
             more stable at detecting the existence of Serial
             cards fitted to the machine.
          b) Removed calls to SerialDev if no serial device
             driver is selected to prevent unexpected crashes.
          c) Fixed bug in file date sorting routine.
             
v0.08     (27th Jul 1998)
          a) Added (and tested) support for the Atomwide dual
             serial port cards. Thanks are due to Chris Manning
             who very kindly loaned me his serial card in order
             to test this facility.
          b) Tidied up some of the menu options to give a neater
             display on pre-Risc PC machines.
          c) Fixed a minor bug which sometimes resulted in an
             incorrect directory listing from the Psion being
             displayed.
          d) Tidied up some internal transfer routines in order
             to make the transfer a bit neater and hopefully much
             more reliable.
          e) Fixed superfluous file occasionally appearing inside
             the Acorn viewer window when looking at empty
             directories on the Psion.
          f) Fixed registration code to work with overseas time
             codes.
             
v0.07     (26th Feb 1998)
          a) Fixed bug in changing baud rate code with SerialDev.
          b) Fixed bug in grabbing directories containing lots of
             files.
          c) Speeded directory grabbing up a bit.
          d) Fixed bug where if no SerialDev was selected they were
             all permanently greyed out and you couldn't turn them
             back on.
          e) Updated Psion ArcLink5.opo slightly.

v0.06a    (20th Feb 1998)
          a) Removed some debugging code inadvertantly left in v0.06
          
v0.06     (18th Feb 1998)
          a) Fixed bug where if a differing baud rate to 19200 was 
             saved in the choices, the baud rate failed to sync with
             Psion next time you load ArcLink5. ArcLink5 now transmits
             the new baud rate on initialisation.
          b) The baud rate is reset to 19200 when you quit ArcLink5
             (this is mainly for debugging purposes, so can be ignored)
          c) Fiddled around with "Resetserial" procedure to fix serial
             port corruption at high speeds (introduced in v0.05)
             
v0.05     (30th Jan 1998) - Archive cover disc (March 1998) version
          a) Speeded up getting directories from Psion.
          b) Added extra configuration options into 'Messages' file
             (see manual for details)
          c) Fixed bug in international routine. Foreign message and
             template files should now work.
          d) Changed menu structure to allow for foreign language menus.
          e) Added iconsprites command to !Run file to ensure that
             ArcLink5 has it's icon, even if it has been run directory
             from a !Boot or application launcher sequence.
          f) Added (hopefully) support for !SerialDev and Atomwide fast
             serial ports (I don't have one, so please give feedback as
             I've coded this blindly from the specs.)
          g) Started to add error checking on the Psion end. If a fatal
             error occurs on the Psion, it should survive and send the
             relevant error code back to the Acorn.
             N.B. This will be improved as ArcLink5 becomes more stable.
          h) Added support for 'inaccessible' files on the Psion. These
             appear an an unknown filetype (file_xxx) in the Acorn filer
             display.
          i) Fixed bug where directory window always appears on left of
             screen instead of where you dragged it to.
          j) Changed default directory opening position to be relative
             to the current screen mode.
          k) Fixed bug where empty directories were displayed containing
             a single file (which didn't actually exist)
          l) Implemented display sorting options in Acorn filer window.
          m) Added 'Abort!' option to main menu as an emergency abort of
             directory transfers.
          n) Implemented copying whole directories from the Psion to the
             Acorn (N.B. Sub-directories are not yet copied!)
          
v0.04a    (19th Jan 1998)
          a) Fixed minor bug in filetype conversion so that the filetype
             is no longer case-sensitive.
          b) Implemented moving files by holding SHIFT down when dragging
             files.
          c) Fixed minor bug which caused a slight delay at the end of
             transferring a new directory from the Psion.

v0.04     (15th Jan 1998)
          a) Extended maximum directory size/depth from 77 to 255 files.
          b) Added user-defined character translations when converting
             filenames to and from Psion<->Acorn filename formats.
             (Codings are inside !ArcLink5.Resources.Trans)
          c) Extended menu structure to allow for 'Display'
             (when supported!)
          d) Extended menu structure to allow for filer 'Options'.
             ('Newer' is not yet supported)
          e) Extended 'unregistered' timeout period from 1st Feb 1998 to
             15th Feb 1998.
          f) Added filetype mapping table to help convert Psion file
             extensions into suitable Acorn filetypes.
          g) Implemented datestamp reading.
          h) Designed a sprite file (and Acorn filetype of 090) for Psion
             OPO files. (Please feel free to improve upon the sprite!)

v0.03     (9th Jan 1998)
          a) Added support for dragging directly from applications to the
             Psion window. This will transfer data straight from the app
             to the Psion. The reverse is also possible, so you could drag
             a file from the Psion window straight into !Zap for instance.
          b) Set filetype icon correctly when dragging a file across to 
             the Psion and the Acorn window is updated.
          c) Fixed bug (icons getting corrupted when given the option to
             delete a long filename file from the Psion)
          d) Improved transfer speed TO Acorn. It is now as fast as going
             TO the Psion. 100k files now transfer in under 30 seconds.
          d) Added code so that all baud rates up to 115200 baud are
             supported (registered version only)
          e) Fixed bug where some directories displayed on the Acorn as
             empty, and gave a "Folder not found" error on the Psion.
          f) Added International support for foreign language messages 
             and templates.
          g) Added 'Choices' menu.
          h) Converted spaces in Psion filenames to "_" (underscore) when
             converting to Acorn file format.
          i) Made Acorn end multi-task while doing transfers
             (optional - controlled by 'Choices.Multitask' menu option)
          j) Added warning before overwriting Acorn files.
          k) Amended filer display to look the same as the Risc OS filer
             windows.
          m) Added option to quit the Psion prog at the same time as the
             Acorn application ('Choices.Quit opo')
          n) Fixed bug in rename so that non Acorn filer characters are
             correctly converted.
          o) Implemented 'Count' for seeing how long Psion files are.
          p) Amended Psion opo so as not to switch the machine off
             through no use when transferring files.
          q) Added SHIFT-doubleclick to load files straight from Psion
             filer window into text editor.
          r) Modified menu widths to look ok on pre-Risc PC machines.
          s) Tested ok on RISC OS 3.1 machines (subject to serial port
             wiring)

v0.02     (3rd Jan 1997)
          - Fixed a few silly bugs and added a couple of features
          
          a) Extended 'Rename' entry field to allow up to 255 characters
             (rather than 10 previously)
          b) Fixed bug in that sending files over 16k to the Psion got
             truncated at 16k
          c) Added support for creating new directories.
          d) Correctly closes filer window when a new device (C: or D:)
             is opened.

v0.01     (2nd Jan 1998) - FIRST BETA TEST VERSION
          Original release version (seems to work ok!)
          - There may be a few bugs, but I thought I'd let people
            play around with it and suggest additional comments.

